From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kitesurf vendor <vendor@kitesurf.invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:34:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Expand horizontal tabs to CSS tab-size stops

HarfRust shapes a tab as an ordinary glyph (usually the font's missing
glyph, painted as a box) with a ~1-space advance. Chrome treats a tab
as invisible whitespace that advances the pen to the next multiple of
tab-size x space-advance from the line start.

Expand tabs at line-commit time, when the pen position within the line
is known: rewrite the tab cluster's advance (and its glyph) to the
tab stop, swapping the glyph for the font's space glyph (no outlines)
when the font has one, so paint draws nothing. Rewriting the
cluster/glyph advances keeps run offsets, line metrics, hit-testing
and selection consistent.

Thread the CSS tab-size value through TextStyle, ResolvedStyle and the
layout Style so explicit tab-size values are honored (default 8).

The shaped clusters and glyphs live in parley_engine, whose half of
this patch adds the mutable accessors the rewrite uses. parley reads
the space glyph with skrifa.
